{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-template-js","path":"/blog/2024-12-21-how-to-use-draft-js-in-react-js/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"excerpt":"Hi Friends 👋, Welcome To aHoisting! To use draft js you have to import  from  and  packages that’s how you can use draft js in react js. Today, I am going to…","html":"<p>Hi Friends 👋,</p>\n<p>Welcome To aHoisting!</p>\n<p>To use draft js you have to import <code class=\"language-text\">draft js</code> from <code class=\"language-text\">Draft.js</code> and <code class=\"language-text\">react-draft-wysiwyg</code> packages that’s how you can use draft js in react js.</p>\n<p>Today, I am going to show you, how to use draft js in react js.</p>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<p>Install the following packages to use draft js in react js.</p>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">npm</code></p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\">npm install draft<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>js react<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>draft<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>wysiwyg\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">yarn</code></p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\">yarn add draft<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>js react<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>draft<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>wysiwyg\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Table of contents</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Install and create a new React app.</li>\n<li>Import react component.</li>\n<li>Create a Component.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Let’s start with the first step.</p>\n<h2>Step 1: Install and create a new React app.</h2>\n<p>First you have to install the React project. You should use <code class=\"language-text\">create-react-app</code> command to create a new React project.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\">npx create<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>react<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>app my<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>app\ncd my<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>app\nnpm start</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Step 2: Import react component.</h2>\n<p>After installing, you have to import your React component.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> React<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> useState <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'react'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> EditorState <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'draft-js'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Editor <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'react-draft-wysiwyg'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token string\">'react-draft-wysiwyg/dist/react-draft-wysiwyg.css'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2>Step 3: Create a Component.</h2>\n<p>You can use <code class=\"language-text\">&lt;Editor/></code> to use draft js in react js.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>div className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"App\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>header className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"App-header\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n        Rich Text Editor Example\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>header<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>Editor\n        editorState<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>editorState<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n        onEditorStateChange<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>setEditorState<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">/</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2>Use draft js example.</h2>\n<p>The below code is an example of a React. You have to import <code class=\"language-text\">draft js</code> from <code class=\"language-text\">'draft-js'</code> and <code class=\"language-text\">'react-draft-wysiwyg'</code> that’s how you can use draft js in react js.</p>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">App.js</code></p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> React<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> useState <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'react'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> EditorState <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'draft-js'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span> Editor <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">'react-draft-wysiwyg'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token string\">'react-draft-wysiwyg/dist/react-draft-wysiwyg.css'</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"token function\">App</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>editorState<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> setEditorState<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token function\">useState</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> EditorState<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">createEmpty</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>div className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"App\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>header className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"App-header\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n        Rich Text Editor Example\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>header<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>Editor\n        editorState<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>editorState<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n        onEditorStateChange<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>setEditorState<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">/</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">default</span> App<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>In the above code example, I have used the <code class=\"language-text\">'react-draft-wysiwyg'</code> to use draft js in react js.</p>\n<p>Check the output of the above code.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/831af1404ab43ece4f9341cf425f3e4f/ec897/use-draft-js.webp\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 33.54430379746836%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/webp;base64,UklGRkYAAABXRUJQVlA4IDoAAADQAgCdASoUAAcALplotFoiqCgoCACYSzgABc6LbFEAAP71B/wWSLzWCVdnr9vyXClARZB7Zfc5gAAA'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"React, use, draft, js\"\n        title=\"React, use, draft, js\"\n        src=\"/static/831af1404ab43ece4f9341cf425f3e4f/8aab1/use-draft-js.webp\"\n        srcset=\"/static/831af1404ab43ece4f9341cf425f3e4f/81b7c/use-draft-js.webp 158w,\n/static/831af1404ab43ece4f9341cf425f3e4f/6ea66/use-draft-js.webp 315w,\n/static/831af1404ab43ece4f9341cf425f3e4f/8aab1/use-draft-js.webp 630w,\n/static/831af1404ab43ece4f9341cf425f3e4f/a70f5/use-draft-js.webp 945w,\n/static/831af1404ab43ece4f9341cf425f3e4f/4ef06/use-draft-js.webp 1260w,\n/static/831af1404ab43ece4f9341cf425f3e4f/ec897/use-draft-js.webp 1366w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>All the best 👍</p>","frontmatter":{"title":"How to use draft js in react js?","tags":["React"],"date":"December 21, 2024","description":"Example of use draft js in react js with step by step tutorial - aHoisting","social_image":{"absolutePath":"/Users/mac/Documents/hoisting/ahoisting/static/media/template/reactjs.jpg"}}},"prev":{"frontmatter":{"title":"How to use cookies in React js?"},"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2024-12-22-how-to-use-cookies-in-react-js/"}},"next":{"frontmatter":{"title":"How to use drag and drop in react js?"},"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2024-12-20-how-to-use-drag-and-drop-in-react-js/"}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/blog/2024-12-21-how-to-use-draft-js-in-react-js/","prevSlug":"/blog/2024-12-22-how-to-use-cookies-in-react-js/","nextSlug":"/blog/2024-12-20-how-to-use-drag-and-drop-in-react-js/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["2555585279","2714594843","3159585216"]}